{
 "note": "Every browser build this project catalogs, all of them from GitHub. Clients that already ship a mod loader, or that are pre-modded (the EaglerForge build and the hacked clients: Astra, WurstX, Resent, DragonX, GX-Client, Pixel) are deliberately absent: mods here come from this project's own injector, so a second loader in the same page would only fight it. Versions with no verifiable GitHub build - 1.18.2 (empty repository) and 1.21.5 / 1.21.11 (no single-file client published that could be checked) - are absent too. Dead sources are removed when their repository disappears; the 26.2/26.3 entries were dropped when the repo that hosted them was deleted.",
 "routes_note": "A version can be served three ways, and the order of preference is: real Java (a JVM in the page runs the official jar, no copy of the game anywhere) > compiled by us from the official source (ahead-of-time, mods baked in) > a prebuilt Eaglercraft-family client, which exists because somebody already did that compile for that version. The prebuilt builds are not 'instead of' the official versions: they *are* those versions, ported to run in a browser, which is why they can be downloaded and played without a JVM.",
 "verified_note": "verified means: fetched over the network, sniffed for the shape of a browser client, and recorded with a size and a sha256 in work/builds/manifest.json.",
